course: dictionary
lesson: 11433
title: Sharp senses and sharp minds
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Acuity is a noun that means sharpness. It is usually used for senses, like eyesight and hearing, or for the mind. When you meet it, look at the words around it for clues. «Her visual acuity is so good that she can read the tiny letters at the bottom of the chart.» The word visual tells you it is about seeing, and the tiny letters show that she sees small details clearly.
explain: Acuity can also describe a sharp mind. «The detective's mental acuity helped her spot the tiny clue that everyone else had missed.» Mental acuity means being quick to notice and understand things. The clue that everyone else missed shows that she was sharper than the others.
explain: Eye tests measure visual acuity. The doctor asks you to read a chart of letters that get smaller and smaller. Doctors say 20/20 (US) or 6/6 (UK) for normal acuity. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if «sharpness of sight» still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Acuity means sharpness, especially of a sense or of the mind.
fact: «Visual acuity» means how clearly you can see small details.
fact: «Mental acuity» means being quick to notice and understand things.
fact: Normal eyesight is written as 20/20 in the US and 6/6 in the UK.
fact: Acuity is usually uncountable, so we say «good acuity», not «an acuity».
exercise: «Her visual acuity is so good that she can read the tiny letters at the bottom of the chart.» What does visual acuity mean here? | How tall she is | *How clearly she can see small details | How fast she can run | How loudly she can hear
exercise: «The detective's mental acuity helped her spot the tiny clue.» What does mental acuity mean? | Being very tired after a long day | Being very strong in the arms | Having a good memory for songs | *Being quick to notice and understand things
exercise: Find and copy the word that means sharpness of a sense: «Owls have excellent acuity at night.» | owls | excellent | *acuity | night
test: The doctor says your eyes are 6/6. What does this show? | *Normal eyesight, measured on a letter chart | The name of the eye doctor | A reading speed test | A type of glasses
test: Complete the sentence: «Ruby solved the puzzle in seconds, which shows her mental ___.» | *acuity | laziness | hunger | carelessness
exam: What is the difference between visual acuity and mental acuity? | *Visual acuity is about sharp senses like sight; mental acuity is about a sharp mind | Visual acuity is about feelings; mental acuity is about food | Visual acuity is a kind of exercise | They mean exactly the same thing
